{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_aa728a78c20745828d6ba859a88c0efb","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_046516d0660add3425b55b7835541c16fe0b6f72128e9e8531aab9679b3f8615","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"egoist/waku@968d42dd38b7 snapshot 623975403b923962","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1feff8680f47f44703b548bdc949355880bce8cc291330a8fd80e48f52cd4700"],"source_ids":["src_d76612cdd51155da99fc20dd87a3646e"],"text":"A browser client lives at apps/web and uses a generated browser transport in packages/waku-client, with types generated from the Rust protocol and a WebSocket client implementing the same handshake, request IDs, subscriptions, deduplication, and replay cursors as the Rust client.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_aa728a78c20745828d6ba859a88c0efb"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_aa728a78c20745828d6ba859a88c0efb","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_085b07a612db2e07162708ae125cc129b2f19a5720035fda27264efdb9064bf6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"egoist/waku@968d42dd38b7 snapshot 623975403b923962","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b557aaa132c65763866b0be86228c285a66cc91ae845830b714aef42f27a333c"],"source_ids":["src_d76612cdd51155da99fc20dd87a3646e"],"text":"The desktop is an RPC client of a standalone waku-daemon; provider sessions run in waku-core behind the authenticated, versioned WebSocket contract in waku-protocol, and the desktop depends on waku-client rather than the daemon implementation.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_aa728a78c20745828d6ba859a88c0efb"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_aa728a78c20745828d6ba859a88c0efb","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_16a73780e69fc98ea02150586325840d298e925cdbdc7d068a5a39ea14d633f6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"egoist/waku@968d42dd38b7 snapshot 623975403b923962","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_15b6de33165ad03d9690733177c649c597a118a2e8df8ee44ca6a002742e7bdb","slc_509dbcd2c09590089b90a68fa1858e24386164be82ddf813c5656e9399ac3165","slc_87587b6ae278ce3901df236f82bc82ad0a12d2970c52080e5c18aa088271d6db","slc_a57530a7a8e96b8a3419a8ceef61a112fa4949cbf1cc2592c68ed13df851196e"],"source_ids":["src_d76612cdd51155da99fc20dd87a3646e"],"text":"Installation is documented per platform: a signed self-updating .dmg on macOS, a curl-piped install script placing files in ~/.local without root on Linux, and a per-user self-updating Setup.exe plus portable .zip on Windows.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:47:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_aa728a78c20745828d6ba859a88c0efb"}
